const beliefDetailsEn=["The Old and New Testaments are divinely inspired Scripture and the authoritative record of God's saving work. They reveal his will, teach the way of salvation in Christ, and provide the standard against which Christian doctrine and experience are evaluated.","There is one God, eternally existing as Father, Son and Holy Spirit. These three coeternal Persons act in unity in creation, redemption and the life of believers; God is infinite, all-knowing, all-powerful and perfectly loving.","The eternal Father is the Creator, Sustainer and Sovereign of all creation. His justice and holiness are inseparable from his mercy, patience and steadfast love, which Jesus and the Holy Spirit also reveal.","The eternal Son became fully human as Jesus Christ without ceasing to be God. Through his sinless life, voluntary death and bodily resurrection he accomplished salvation; he ministers for believers and will return to restore all things.","The Holy Spirit is a divine Person active in creation and redemption. He inspired biblical writers, convicts people of sin, brings renewal, gives spiritual gifts and guides the church in harmony with Scripture.","God created the world in six literal days and rested on the seventh, establishing the Sabbath as a lasting memorial of creation. Humanity was created in God's image and entrusted with responsibility for the natural world.","Men and women were made in God's image with freedom and responsibility. Sin damaged human nature and brought death, yet God acts through Christ and the Holy Spirit to restore his image in repentant people.","Human history forms part of the conflict between Christ and Satan over God's character and rule. Evil entered the world through rebellion, but Christ sends the Spirit and faithful angels to sustain his people.","Christ's obedient life, substitutionary death and bodily resurrection provide the only sufficient atonement for human sin. His victory over evil discloses God's justice and mercy and brings believers hope beyond death.","Salvation comes through God's grace in Jesus Christ, received by faith rather than earned through good works. The Spirit leads people to repentance, justification, new birth and growth in holiness.","Because Christ has defeated evil, believers need not remain captive to fear or the burdens of their past. Prayer, Scripture, worship, fellowship and compassionate service shape continued growth in his likeness.","The church is the community of believers who confess Jesus Christ as Lord. It gathers for worship, biblical instruction, communion, mutual care and mission, with Christ himself as its head.","The worldwide church includes all who truly believe in Christ. Adventists describe an end-time remnant that keeps God's commandments, trusts Jesus and proclaims the three angels' messages and the coming judgment.","Believers form one body in Christ across differences in ethnicity, language, social position and background. The unity given by the Spirit calls them to serve one another without discrimination or partiality.","Baptism by immersion expresses faith in Christ's death and resurrection and a commitment to new life. It follows personal repentance, biblical instruction and a conscious confession of faith.","The Lord's Supper remembers Christ's sacrifice and proclaims his return. Self-examination and foot washing express renewed cleansing, humble service and reconciliation within the Christian community.","The Holy Spirit gives members different gifts for service and the common good. Teaching, leadership, compassion, proclamation and other ministries strengthen the church in truth and love.","Adventists believe the prophetic gift appeared in the ministry of Ellen G. White. Her writings offer guidance and correction, while the Bible remains the final standard for testing teaching and experience.","God's moral law, summarized by the Ten Commandments, expresses love for God and others. It identifies sin and the need for a Savior; obedience is the fruit of grace, not a way to earn salvation.","The seventh-day Sabbath, observed from sunset Friday to sunset Saturday, is set apart for rest, worship and service. It commemorates creation, celebrates redemption and anticipates God's future kingdom.","Human time, resources, gifts and possessions belong ultimately to God. Stewardship calls for their responsible use, including generous service, tithes and offerings in support of gospel mission.","Christian conduct should reflect Christ in choices, relationships and care for the body. Adventists emphasize wholesome recreation, modesty, rest, exercise, healthful food and abstinence from harmful substances.","Adventist teaching regards marriage as a lifelong covenant between a man and a woman, marked by mutual love and responsibility. Families are encouraged to nurture children in faith, while the church welcomes single and married members.","Christ ministers as High Priest in the heavenly sanctuary. Adventists connect the 2,300-day prophecy in Daniel with an investigative judgment beginning in 1844 as part of the final removal of sin.","Christ's second coming will be personal, visible, literal and worldwide. The righteous dead will rise, and believers are called to live expectantly rather than attempt to predict the date.","Death is understood as an unconscious state until resurrection. God alone possesses inherent immortality, and eternal life is given to the redeemed through Christ.","The millennium is Christ's thousand-year reign with his saints between the first and second resurrections. The final judgment will bring sin and evil to an end.","God promises a renewed earth where the redeemed live with him. Death, suffering and sin will have ceased, and all creation will display God's love."];
const beliefContextEn=["Scripture is also the test of spiritual experience and the trustworthy record of God's acts in history.","Though God exceeds human comprehension, he makes himself known and is worthy of worship and service.","The Father's character is not opposed to Christ's compassion: each reveals the same divine love and holiness.","Jesus experienced human temptation, revealed God's character through his ministry and now intercedes for humanity.","The Spirit strengthens Christian witness and transforms those who respond to his work.","The Sabbath gives the created week its enduring rhythm and reminds us to care for creation.","Human beings depend on God for life, and redemption restores their capacity to love and serve.","The controversy involves real consequences for the world, yet divine help remains available.","The resurrection proclaims Christ's victory and assures believers of ultimate deliverance.","New life includes adoption into God's family and the assurance of salvation in Christ.","Christian growth involves attending to physical, mental, social and spiritual needs.","The church is also portrayed as God's family, Christ's body and his beloved bride.","Each believer is invited to participate personally in the worldwide gospel witness.","Unity does not erase personal differences; it makes loving fellowship possible across them.","Immersion symbolizes forgiveness, union with Christ and receiving the Holy Spirit.","Foot washing especially expresses humility and readiness to serve others.","Different gifts cooperate to build a mature, united Christian community.","Her writings are not a replacement for Scripture, which judges every claimed revelation.","The Spirit writes God's law of love upon believers' hearts.","Joyful Sabbath observance strengthens communion with God and the community.","Faithful stewardship resists selfishness and seeks the welfare of others.","Christians are encouraged to choose habits that promote health, purity and joy.","The church is called to support all families with care and compassionate guidance.","This teaching interprets the ancient sanctuary as a type of Christ's heavenly ministry.","The time of the second coming is unknown, so readiness is a continuing calling.","The resurrection of the unrighteous is understood to occur after the millennium.","At its close, the holy city descends and God's judgment finally removes evil.","The great controversy ends with reconciliation, righteousness and everlasting life."];

const scriptureNames={'Ps.':'Psalms','Prov.':'Proverbs','Isa.':'Isaiah','John':'John','Thess.':'Thessalonians','Tim.':'Timothy','Heb.':'Hebrews','Peter':'Peter','Gen.':'Genesis','Deut.':'Deuteronomy','Matt.':'Matthew','Cor.':'Corinthians','Eph.':'Ephesians','Rev.':'Revelation','Luke':'Luke','Dan.':'Daniel','Rom.':'Romans','Phil.':'Philippians','Col.':'Colossians','Sam.':'Samuel','Acts':'Acts','Chron.':'Chronicles','Exod.':'Exodus','Ezek.':'Ezekiel','Job':'Job','Mark':'Mark','Gal.':'Galatians','Jer.':'Jeremiah','Hab.':'Habakkuk','Titus':'Titus','Mic.':'Micah','Jude':'Jude','Lev.':'Leviticus','Haggai':'Haggai','Mal.':'Malachi','Eccl.':'Ecclesiastes','James':'James','Num.':'Numbers','Amos':'Amos','Joel':'Joel','Zec.':'Zechariah'};
function beliefReferenceButtons(source){
 let lastBook='',lastChapter='',items=[],seen=new Set();
 for(const chunk of source.split(';')){
   const part=chunk.trim();if(!part)continue;
   const match=part.match(/^(?:(\d)\s+)?([A-Za-z.]+)\s+(.+)$/);
   let portion=part;
   if(match && scriptureNames[match[2]]){lastBook=(match[1]?match[1]+' ':'')+scriptureNames[match[2]];portion=match[3];lastChapter=''}
   if(!lastBook)continue;
   for(const section of portion.split(/,\s*/)){
     const p=section.trim();if(!p)continue;
     let chapter='',verses='';
     if(p.includes(':')){const parts=p.split(':');chapter=parts[0];verses=parts[1];lastChapter=chapter}
     else if(lastChapter && /^\d+$/.test(p)){chapter=lastChapter;verses=p}
     else {chapter=p;lastChapter=''}
     if(!/^\d{1,3}(?:-\d{1,3})?$/.test(chapter)|| (verses&&!/^\d{1,3}(?:-\d{1,3})?$/.test(verses)))continue;
     // The verse API requires a verse expression. A whole-chapter reference starts at verse 1.
     const ref=lastBook+' '+chapter+(verses?':'+verses:'');
     const id=ref.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g,' ');
     if(seen.has(id))continue;seen.add(id);
     const label=lastBook+' '+chapter+(verses?':'+verses:'');
     items.push('<button type="button" class="ref-link" data-scripture="'+esc(ref)+'" title="'+L('Lees Bybelteks','Read passage')+'">'+esc(label)+' ↗</button>');
   }
 }
 return items.join('');
}

function about(){const groups=h.beliefGroups;let n=0;layout(header(L('Ons identiteit','Our identity'),L('Oor die Sewendedag-Adventistekerk','About the Seventh-day Adventist Church'),L('Ontdek ons geskiedenis, sending en 28 Bybelgegronde geloofsoortuigings.','Explore our history, mission and 28 Bible-based fundamental beliefs.'))+`<section class="section section-light"><div class="container narrow longform"><span class="eyebrow">${L('Ons geloof','Our faith')}</span><h2>${L('Jesus Christus staan sentraal.','Jesus Christ is central.')}</h2><p>${L('Sewendedag-Adventiste is Christene wat die Bybel as die grondslag van geloof en praktyk aanvaar. Die naam Adventis verwys na die verwagting van Jesus Christus se wederkoms, terwyl die sewende dag, Saterdag, aan God se Sabbat herinner.','Seventh-day Adventists are Christians who accept the Bible as the foundation of faith and practice. Adventist refers to the expected return of Jesus Christ, while the seventh day, Saturday, recalls God’s Sabbath.')}</p><p>${L('Die beweging het gedurende die negentiende eeu gevorm en in 1863 as ’n georganiseerde kerk ontwikkel. Vandag bestaan dit uit gemeentes regoor die wêreld, met ’n sterk fokus op aanbidding, Bybelonderrig, gesondheidsorg, opvoeding en hulp aan mense in nood.','The movement took shape in the nineteenth century and was organized as a church in 1863. Today it has congregations around the world, emphasizing worship, biblical education, health, schooling and compassionate service.')}</p><p>${L('Die 28 geloofsoortuigings hieronder word in ses studietemas aangebied. Maak enige onderwerp oop vir ’n uitgebreide verduideliking, Bybelverwysings en ’n vraag om verder oor na te dink.','The 28 beliefs are arranged in six study themes. Expand any topic for a fuller explanation, Bible references and a study question.')}</p></div></section><section class="section section-warm"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">${L('Die 28 geloofsoortuigings','28 fundamental beliefs')}</span><h2>${L('Verdiep jou begrip, een onderwerp op ’n slag.','Explore each belief more deeply.')}</h2></div></div>${groups.map(group=>`<div class="belief-section"><h2>${esc(L(group.af,group.en))}</h2><div class="belief-accordion">${group.items.map(([af,en,da,de])=>{let i=n++;const completeRefs=sourceReferenceLists[i];return `<details class="belief-detail"><summary><span>${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><strong>${esc(L(af,en))}</strong><span class="expand-mark">+</span></summary><div class="belief-detail-body"><p>${esc(L(da,de))}</p><p class="belief-expanded">${esc(lang()==='af'?detailedBeliefsAf[i]:beliefDetailsEn[i])}</p><p class="belief-expanded">${esc(lang()==='af'?fullerBeliefsAf[i]:beliefContextEn[i])}</p><p>${L('Om hierdie leerstelling te bestudeer, lees die verwante Skrifgedeeltes in hul oorspronklike konteks. Vra hoe die teks aansluit by die breër boodskap van verlossing deur Jesus Christus en hoe dit in die lewe van ’n gelowige gestalte kry.','Study this doctrine by reading the related Scripture passages in their context. Consider how each text connects to salvation through Jesus Christ and practical Christian living.')}</p><h4>${L('Lees in die Bybel','Read in Scripture')}</h4><div class="ref-list">${beliefReferenceButtons(completeRefs)}</div><div class="study-question"><strong>${L('Dink verder','Reflect')}</strong><p>${esc(lang()==='af'?promptsAf[i%4]:promptsEn[i%4])}</p></div></div></details>`}).join('')}</div></div>`).join('')}</div></section>`)}
